# Every resource from NWS_Hawaii_Resource_Map.md, tagged with category
# (→ which fetch/ module owns it), tier (→ config/tiers.yaml), and a
# local_path_template following nws_plan.md Section 1's rule:
#
#   https://<host>/<path>/<name>.<ext>
#   -> <base_dir>/<host>/<path>/<name>/<name>_current.<ext>          (live)
#   -> <base_dir>/<host>/<path>/<name>/archive/<MM-DD-YYYY>/<name>_<TIMESTAMP>.<ext>  (history)
#
# base_dir = /home/rootrecord/Database/WEATHER/Hawai'i/hfo
# path_resolver.py derives local_path_template mechanically from `url` at
# runtime for any resource that follows the general rule — the templates
# below are recorded for the handful of URLs where the name/extension
# isn't obvious from the URL alone (query strings, extensionless paths).
#
# method: api (structured JSON, primary) | scrape (product.php HTML, fallback
#         or only option) | image (static gif/png/jpg/tif) | json (non-product
#         structured API, e.g. alerts/points/CurrentStorms)

